Subject: Cantor Field Attention Resource Bounds P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 43912daf-b18a-43d1-b14f-4a04329d175a
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-18_field_attention_resource_bounds\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Field_Attention_Resource_Bounds_P0.exploded.sop

& [Problem] is that bounded semantic cardinality does not bound memory context transport duration or evidence volume

& [Decision] is explicit byte and time ceilings with fail-closed exact preservation
  + byte counts use UTF-8 so cross-platform behavior is deterministic
  + no accepted input is truncated normalized summarized retried or repaired
  + generous P0 ceilings cover the current five-element corpus while remaining finite
  + response body digests retain failure identity without persisting arbitrary text
  + disabled proxies and redirects preserve the admitted loopback endpoint after URL validation

& [Alternatives] are rejected
  - character counts are rejected because encoded memory and transport costs vary
  - token counts alone are rejected because parsing and evidence allocation happen outside tokenization
  - implicit library defaults are rejected because they are not inspectable contracts
  - unlimited local-loopback trust is rejected because local software can still malfunction

& [Nonclaim] is that these budgets do not establish adversarial production hardening or semantic quality
